# DECOMPOSITION.in - fullcell_physical (25 reactions). Basis: docs/KINETICS_TABLE.md
# anode SEI (1E-4 base-case values) + cathode conversions (PLACEHOLDERS for AIMD)
# format: <NAME> <nChannels> then per channel: sigma k0 Ea alpha E0
# ---- anode -----------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- anode: physically based (cases/anode_physical, KINETICS_TABLE.md) ----
# Plating / PlatingSEI are supplied by the BV block (anode_kinetics bv); the
# two entries below are parsed but ignored. FSI / SFO / SOL: CE-anchored
# (CE 0.998, Yu 2022) with candidate multiplicities of the 10x10x30 box:
# k_FSI 19, k_SFO 0.19, k_SOL 0.25 s^-1 per adjacent site [V-derived].
# SOL2 (F5DEE on Li2O): SAME CE-anchored prefactor as SOL (0.25 s^-1 per
# adjacent site) with the Tan 2024 barrier 0.364 eV as the RELATIVE attenuation
# of the Li2O route vs the Li route (barrierless on Li): k = 0.25 exp(-0.364/kT)
# = 1.8e-7 s^-1 [V-derived]. The previous kT/h prefactor (6.2e12) gave 4.5e6
# s^-1 per site: an inexhaustible sink that buried the anode under F/F5D once
# the first O sites appeared (fullcell_physical run 1, 2950 SEI sites in 8
# cycles). Upper bound for sensitivity: Ea 0.000 (Li2O as reactive as Li).
Plating 1
1 1E-4 0.000 0.0 -3.04
PlatingSEI 1
1 1E-4 0.000 0.0 -3.04
FSI 1
1 19 0.000 0.0 -3.04
SFO 1
1 0.19 0.000 0.0 -3.04
SOL 1
1 0.25 0.000 0.0 -3.04
SOL2 1
1 0.25 0.364 0.0 -3.04
# ---- cathode cascade, Butler-Volmer at the cathode potential (cathode_kinetics bv)
# format: sigma k0 Ea alpha E0. k0 per site from exchange current densities
# (k0 = i0 A_site / e, A_site 4e-20 m2): high plateau iH,0 = 10 A/m2 -> 2.5 s^-1,
# low plateau iL,0 = 5 A/m2 -> 1.25 s^-1 (Marinescu, Zhang, Offer, PCCP 2016,
# Table 1) [V]. E0 = standard potentials of Kumaresan, Mikhaylik, White, JES
# 2008, Table II: 2.39 (S8 -> S8^2-), 2.24 (-> S4^2-, limiting of S6/S4 steps),
# 2.04 (-> S2^2-), 2.01 (-> S^2-) [V-assumed]. alpha = -0.5 for reductions
# (favoured when V_cat < E0), +0.5 for the reverse oxidations (alpha 0.5,
# Kumaresan 2008 Table II). Kumaresan's own i0 set (0.49, 4.7e-3, 4.9e-5,
# 4.9e-8 s^-1 per site) is the sensitivity bound (KINETICS_TABLE.md sec. 4).
cat_S8_red 1
1 2.5 0.000 -0.5 2.39
cat_Li2S8_red 1
1 2.5 0.000 -0.5 2.24
cat_Li4S8_red 1
1 1.25 0.000 -0.5 2.04
cat_Li8S8_red 1
1 1.25 0.000 -0.5 2.01
cat_Li16S8_ox 1
1 1.25 0.000 0.5 2.01
cat_Li8S8_ox 1
1 1.25 0.000 0.5 2.04
cat_Li4S8_ox 1
1 2.5 0.000 0.5 2.24
cat_Li2S8_ox 1
1 2.5 0.000 0.5 2.39
# ---- polysulfide dissolution (cathode, any V) : PLACEHOLDER ---------------
# per-site k0 [1/s]; Li2S8 > Li4S8 (Li2S4 marginally soluble); Li8S8/Li16S8
# insoluble -> no dissolution channel. Rauh 1977 / Mikhaylik 2004: S as Li2Sx
# exceeds 10 M in ethers, so high-order dissolution is fast.
cat_diss_Li2S8 1
1 0.05 0.000 0.0 0.0
cat_diss_Li4S8 1
1 0.02 0.000 0.0 0.0
# ---- re-precipitation on empty cathode sites (any V) : PLACEHOLDER --------
# rate per empty site = k0 * c_x, c_x = N_dis[x]/reservoir_sites (mean field).
# k_diss/k_prec sets the dissolved fraction at steady state (calibrate ratio,
# not each value). Marinescu et al. JES 165 (2018) A6107: precipitation
# constant k_p. cat_prec_Li2S6 is the 2 Li2S6 -> Li2S8 + Li2S4 disproportionation.
cat_prec_Li2S8 1
1 5.0 0.000 0.0 0.0
cat_prec_Li2S6 1
1 5.0 0.000 0.0 0.0
cat_prec_Li2S4 1
1 5.0 0.000 0.0 0.0
# ---- polysulfide shuttle at the Li surface (any V) : PLACEHOLDER, step 1 --
# rate per surface Li0 site = k0 * c_x (mean field). Calibrate against the
# Mikhaylik-Akridge shuttle factor f_c = k_s q_H [S]/I (exp. ~1.1 to 4,
# JES 151 (2004) A1969) and target CE (0.95-0.99 with LiNO3, 0.6-0.9 without).
# 2026-09-22 step 2: ks = 0.53 h^-1 (Mikhaylik and Akridge 2004, 298 K) converted
# to a per Li0-surface-site rate, ks * reservoir_sites / N_surf = 0.009 s^-1
# (10x10x30 box) -> 0.01 / 0.01 / 0.004 [V-derived].
# 2026-09-21 calibration step 1: the original 0.5/0.5/0.2 gave CE_shuttle
# 0.28 to 0.65 and 128 anode deposits in 10 half-cycles (6x6x24 box, brakes
# on, cathode fix in); 0.05/0.05/0.02 gave CE_shuttle 0.63 to 0.80, i.e. the
# no-LiNO3 literature range, with 15 deposits. Adopted as the working value.
# NOT a final calibration (single seed, small box).
sh_Li2S8 1
1 0.01 0.000 0.0 0.0
sh_Li2S6 1
1 0.01 0.000 0.0 0.0
sh_Li2S4 1
1 0.004 0.000 0.0 0.0
# ---- CEI: FSI reduced by long-chain polysulfides (cathode_surface, any V) --
# rate per FSI surface site = k0 * c_x, c_x = N_dis[x]/reservoir_sites (mean
# field, same footing as the shuttle sh_Li2Sx rates 0.5/0.5/0.2 per Li0 site).
# PLACEHOLDER magnitude, relative reasoning: [SF26] Fig. 3a, pure-LiFSI cell
# loses ~85 % of its capacity within ~8 cycles at C/10, i.e. the FSI path
# removes a large fraction of the long-chain inventory per cycle. With ~20 FSI
# surface sites against ~300 Li0 surface sites (10x10x30 box), k0 = 1.0 gives
# the CEI path roughly one tenth of the shuttle's initial event share; raise
# toward 5 to reproduce the few-cycle collapse of [SF26]. Li2S8 and Li2S6 are
# given the same k0 (both "long chain" in [SF26]; no chain-length resolution).
# TODO calibrate against [SF26] Fig. 3a once the S8-unit cascade is in place.
cei_FSI_Li2S8 1
1 1.0 0.000 0.0 0.0
cei_FSI_Li2S6 1
1 1.0 0.000 0.0 0.0
# ---- CEI: F5DEE vs polysulfides. DISABLED (sigma 0): no evidence yet -------
cei_F5DEE_Li2S8 1
0 0.1 0.000 0.0 0.0
